1
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:49,199
(Episode 5)

2
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:50,960
(This is a work of fiction.)

3
00:01:56,960 --> 00:01:59,360
Platinum.

4
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:00,560
Darn it!

5
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:03,440
- Another gold card. - Should we talk to the manager?

6
00:02:09,040 --> 00:02:10,200
This card won't go through.

7
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:12,040
Is this why you called me so urgently?

8
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:13,800
And this month's allowance...

9
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,000
hasn't come through.

10
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:17,040
Hey!

11
00:02:17,041 --> 00:02:18,480
You said it was an emergency, that you were dying.

12
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:19,640
That's why I rushed over.

13
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:22,160
The card was declined, I couldn't pay the bill.

14
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:24,160
Won't I have to go to jail? Isn't that an emergency?

15
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:28,720
Hey, give her that bill from just now.

16
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,600
I should have known.

17
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:51,280
What else do you ever talk to me about besides money?

18
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:57,720
I give you so much money. Where does it all go?

19
00:02:58,240 --> 00:02:59,800
How did you max out your credit card?

20
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:01,760
Once you give me the money, it's mine.

21
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:03,320
It's none of your business how I spend it.

22
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:14,520
Can we...

23
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:17,400
just have a proper meal together one day?

24
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:22,720
Honey, I'm back.

25
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:25,640
Fine, let's invite Chiu to join us too.

26
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:27,720
What took you so long?

27
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,960
I ate so much. I had to clear my system.

28
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:37,440
Are you Nancy's niece?

29
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:39,240
Hello. You can call me Chiu.

30
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:46,040
Is he the one you're spending your money on?

31
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:48,520
It's none of your business.

32
00:03:49,040 --> 00:03:50,440
None of my business?

33
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,160
I'm the one giving you that money.

34
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:55,280
It's not for your useless boyfriends.

35
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:57,200
You have failed so many times.

36
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:59,160
Yet, why do you keep repeating the same mistakes?

37
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:01,360
I'm not giving you any more money to support your boyfriends.

38
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:04,680
You owe me. I deserve that money.

39
00:04:04,760 --> 00:04:06,079
Don't get too worked up.

40
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:07,760
- It's bad for your health. - Excuse me, folks.

41
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:09,520
Would you mind taking this outside?

42
00:04:09,600 --> 00:04:11,400
Because your volume is...

43
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:19,880
If I give you the money,

44
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:23,920
but you never see me again,

45
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:28,760
would you still want it?

46
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:34,760
Fine, just give me the money. Cash is more practical anyway.

47
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:00,160
Hello, Ms. Yau.

48
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:26,320
Where's my master?

49
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:28,120
He went to lunch with Mrs. Yeung.

50
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:38,560
I've negotiated with the King of Hell for you.

51
00:05:41,240 --> 00:05:42,520
How long can I stay?

52
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:48,480
Three days.

53
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:51,640
Sorry, I did my best.

54
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,160
I've handled your will for you.

55
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:56,400
I've sorted out the issues between you and your wife.

56
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:58,240
I even got your son to reconcile. I've done everything!

57
00:05:58,320 --> 00:05:59,880
And you're telling me it's only three days?

58
00:05:59,960 --> 00:06:01,879
I didn't want this either.

59
00:06:01,880 --> 00:06:03,280
I've talked until my mouth is dry.

60
00:06:03,360 --> 00:06:05,840
I gave him all my money, but he still said only three days.

61
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:07,240
You promised me!

62
00:06:07,320 --> 00:06:08,600
I did my part.

63
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,880
But he wouldn't budge. There's nothing I can do.

64
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:20,640
Leave!

65
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:21,840
What?

66
00:06:22,160 --> 00:06:23,160
Leave!

67
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:25,360
I told you to leave!

68
00:06:25,840 --> 00:06:28,520
Human or ghost, you're all just using me!

69
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:30,680
You're all jerks! Leave!

70
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:00,680
For anything urgent,

71
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:03,280
bring a mirror to my grave to find me.

72
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:23,160
Excuse me.

73
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:25,400
Excuse me.

74
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:27,440
Where is the 10 Kings' Hall?

75
00:07:27,520 --> 00:07:29,280
The place with the 10 kings.

76
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:44,960
(The 10 Yama Courts)

77
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:51,720
Yama, come out right now!

78
00:07:52,440 --> 00:07:54,280
I've donated so much money and done so many good deeds.

79
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:55,880
I should have many more years of life.

80
00:07:55,960 --> 00:07:57,640
It's impossible that it's only three days.

81
00:07:57,720 --> 00:07:59,360
You've made a mistake. Come out!

82
00:07:59,440 --> 00:08:01,320
Recalculate it in front of me!

83
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:03,640
Come out! I said come out!

84
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:12,440
If you don't come out and explain,

85
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:14,080
I'll smash all your statues!

86
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:34,439
Impudent woman!

87
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:35,960
How dare you disrupt the 10 Kings' Hall?

88
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:39,160
I want to see Yama.

89
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:40,840
Not nameless nobodies like you.

90
00:08:40,920 --> 00:08:42,040
Tell him to come out now!

91
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:43,520
Nameless nobodies?

92
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:46,840
You shrew! We'll send you on your way right now.

93
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:53,400
Do you like playing with me?

94
00:08:53,480 --> 00:08:54,480
I do.

95
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:56,479
Then let's play together forever.

96
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:57,800
Let's never be apart.

97
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:02,200
Where are you going now?

98
00:09:03,000 --> 00:09:04,320
I'll be back soon.

99
00:09:04,760 --> 00:09:07,000
Is going out more important than your daughter?

100
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:09,080
It's fine as long as you're here.

101
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:10,160
This is your responsibility.

102
00:09:10,161 --> 00:09:11,520
You gave birth to her, so accept it.

103
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:12,920
I never said I wanted to have her.

104
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:14,800
You were the one who said I couldn't have an abortion.

105
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:16,280
You were already four months along then.

106
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:18,360
Abortion is dangerous, you know?

107
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:20,320
You forced me into this.

108
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:23,160
You're the one who wanted her, not me.

109
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Si!

110
00:09:25,280 --> 00:09:26,960
Si!

111
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:45,280
Does Mom not want me?

112
00:09:46,080 --> 00:09:48,400
No, she's just still young.

113
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:52,160
Grandpa and Grandma will love and protect you.

114
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:53,240
Do you understand?

115
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:55,160
Don't be mad at your mother.

116
00:09:58,240 --> 00:10:00,280
I have a lot of new friends.

117
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:02,040
What's your name?

118
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:03,320
I'm Piggy.

119
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:05,240
Piggy is a silly name.

120
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:09,600
Yam Yam, why are you coughing?

121
00:10:09,680 --> 00:10:11,040
Did you not drink enough water?

122
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:14,040
Honey!

123
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:15,600
- What's wrong? - Look, is there a fire?

124
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,320
Let me take a look.

125
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:22,360
The fire is huge!

126
00:10:22,560 --> 00:10:24,760
Quick, hide in the bathroom! Hurry, come!

127
00:10:25,720 --> 00:10:26,720
- Hurry! - Hurry!

128
00:10:27,240 --> 00:10:29,880
Hurry, honey, hurry!

129
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:31,880
Here, come on.

130
00:10:32,160 --> 00:10:34,080
- Yam Yam, hold this. Hold it. - Get down.

131
00:10:34,160 --> 00:10:35,160
Get down.

132
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:38,360
Don't be afraid. Grandma is here.

133
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:41,600
I'll protect you. You'll be fine.

134
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:43,400
Let's hang in there a bit longer.

135
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:44,960
Someone will save us soon.

136
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:47,480
Be a good girl, Yam Yam.

137
00:11:13,120 --> 00:11:15,720
This is the first time someone has looked for me like this.

138
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:19,080
Interesting.

139
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:27,360
If we're going to settle the score,

140
00:11:29,560 --> 00:11:32,080
I'll take my time settling it with you.

141
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:34,240
Your Majesty.

142
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:37,360
This shrew is so arrogant. She should be punished severely.

143
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:39,120
Exactly.

144
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:41,440
She even called us nameless nobodies.

145
00:11:44,760 --> 00:11:46,280
Did she really call you nameless nobodies?

146
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:50,240
Good names.

147
00:11:51,560 --> 00:11:55,000
From now on, you're Nameless, and you're Nobody.

148
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:57,200
Do you like them?

149
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:01,880
We do.

150
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:08,360
Yau Yam Yam, since you like things clear-cut,

151
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:09,960
I'll give you exactly that.

152
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:19,400
Nameless, Nobody, let's go.

153
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,680
Yama, come out here!

154
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,200
Come out!

155
00:12:54,760 --> 00:12:56,040
Come out!

156
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:06,360
(Grave of Shek Chung)

157
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:10,680
Come out.

158
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:12,920
Please.

159
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,520
Tell King Yama to come out and see me now.

160
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:24,360
I want to settle the score with him.

161
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:28,560
Stop pestering him.

162
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:30,640
It's just a waste of time.

163
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:34,200
You should make good use of these last three days.

164
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:36,800
Do what you want to do...

165
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:38,840
and see the people you want to see.

166
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,360
Three days isn't enough.

167
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:43,720
Either you take me down to find him,

168
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:45,040
or you bring him up here to see me.

169
00:13:50,160 --> 00:13:51,160
What's wrong?

170
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:54,480
You just got back. Are you out of energy already?

171
00:13:57,600 --> 00:13:58,720
I'm not out of energy.

172
00:14:02,480 --> 00:14:03,480
It's just...

173
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:06,280
I'm about to be reincarnated.

174
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:08,960
This time I've come to see you,

175
00:14:10,160 --> 00:14:11,800
it should be the last time.

176
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:18,600
So what if you're being reincarnated?

177
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:22,400
You said you would help me.

178
00:14:24,760 --> 00:14:25,880
Let me tell you,

179
00:14:26,560 --> 00:14:28,520
you can't leave until you've settled your debt with me.

180
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,440
I've come to see you this time...

181
00:14:35,160 --> 00:14:36,520
not just to say goodbye,

182
00:14:37,280 --> 00:14:39,280
but also to remind you of something.

183
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:43,160
If you want a better life in the netherworld,

184
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:45,960
burn more funeral money for yourself.

185
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:47,360
I can sense...

186
00:14:47,361 --> 00:14:51,040
that you don't get along with your family.

187
00:14:51,960 --> 00:14:53,680
And you've offended so many people.

188
00:14:54,880 --> 00:14:56,720
I doubt anyone will burn any offerings for you.

189
00:14:58,040 --> 00:15:00,320
It's safer to rely on yourself.

190
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:06,080
I've opened a bank account for you down there.

191
00:15:06,920 --> 00:15:09,360
Whenever you burn offerings for yourself,

192
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:11,480
write your name clearly.

193
00:15:11,560 --> 00:15:12,920
Then you'll definitely receive it.

194
00:15:14,200 --> 00:15:18,280
As you saw, everything in the netherworld costs money.

195
00:15:19,160 --> 00:15:21,840
Poor ghosts have a miserable time.

196
00:15:26,400 --> 00:15:28,040
If I really do go down there,

197
00:15:29,400 --> 00:15:31,040
how long will I have to wait to be reincarnated?

198
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:35,000
The queue for reincarnation is very long.

199
00:15:35,920 --> 00:15:38,520
If you want to be faster, you have to pay more.

200
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:42,199
But you must serve all your punishments...

201
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:43,480
before you can go.

202
00:15:44,120 --> 00:15:47,080
In short, it takes a long time.

203
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:53,320
You're lying to me.

204
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:56,000
You're breaking your promise.

205
00:15:57,800 --> 00:15:59,160
Blaming me won't help.

206
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:02,120
You should think about the practical problems.

207
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:06,800
Honestly, I'm afraid you won't even make it to reincarnation.

208
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:09,840
Why?

209
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:12,480
Doesn't everyone get to reincarnate?

210
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:17,720
If no one in the mortal world remembers you...

211
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:19,880
or misses you,

212
00:16:20,400 --> 00:16:24,240
you'll turn into fragments in the netherworld.

213
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:27,160
I'm sorry, Chung.

214
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:39,760
I'm sorry too.

215
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:42,360
I have to go.

216
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:46,200
Live a good life.

217
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:50,160
If we are destined,

218
00:17:54,160 --> 00:17:57,720
let's be husband and wife again in the next life.

219
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:02,000
Goodbye.

220
00:18:58,680 --> 00:19:00,240
Have you reincarnated yet?

221
00:19:03,840 --> 00:19:05,280
If I die too,

222
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:08,840
will you all turn into fragments?

223
00:19:13,520 --> 00:19:17,200
I'll give Aunt a lot of money before I die.

224
00:19:17,880 --> 00:19:20,960
I'll tell her to burn lots of joss paper for you every year.

225
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:23,560
If she doesn't, I'll cut her off.

226
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:27,919
(Cheng Fai Cho and Ho Oi Yuk)

227
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:29,720
I miss you all so much.

228
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:32,760
Amber?

229
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:36,960
So you have relatives here too?

230
00:19:39,960 --> 00:19:41,120
Your parents?

231
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:45,600
Hello, sir, ma'am.

232
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:48,040
I'm Yin Pan. You can call me Ben.

233
00:19:48,840 --> 00:19:50,280
I really like your daughter.

234
00:19:51,640 --> 00:19:52,960
I'll treat her well.

235
00:19:54,440 --> 00:19:55,720
Don't talk nonsense.

236
00:19:58,240 --> 00:19:59,600
Why don't you visit my mom too?

237
00:20:04,080 --> 00:20:05,919
(Lui Ching Han)

238
00:20:05,920 --> 00:20:08,960
Mom, this is Amber,

239
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:10,320
the woman I like.

240
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:12,400
Unfortunately, she doesn't like me.

241
00:20:13,480 --> 00:20:15,960
Help me out. I can't win her over.

242
00:20:16,440 --> 00:20:17,440
I'm counting on you.

243
00:20:25,040 --> 00:20:26,720
Did your mom like Korean things?

244
00:20:27,320 --> 00:20:29,520
Yes, she was a total fangirl.

245
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,640
When I was little, she even told me my dad was Korean.

246
00:20:34,360 --> 00:20:36,040
But I just went along with whatever she said.

247
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:38,800
I've never met my dad anyway.

248
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,320
She was very afraid of being alone.

249
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:48,200
So I come to keep her company whenever I have time.

250
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,400
Next time I visit my mom,

251
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:53,480
I'll visit your parents too.

252
00:20:55,920 --> 00:20:56,920
No need.

253
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:58,280
It's on the way.

254
00:20:58,920 --> 00:21:01,560
You're so busy. They must be bored.

255
00:21:08,840 --> 00:21:10,720
Your car is fixed. Shall I take you to get it?

256
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:26,960
I can tell you don't get along well with your family.

257
00:21:27,040 --> 00:21:29,040
Probably no one will burn joss paper for you.

258
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:31,200
It's safer to rely on yourself.

259
00:21:31,280 --> 00:21:33,000
Let's handle the important stuff first.

260
00:21:34,040 --> 00:21:35,040
What?

261
00:21:35,360 --> 00:21:36,520
You're free, right?

262
00:21:45,720 --> 00:21:48,200
I want all the joss paper here.

263
00:21:48,280 --> 00:21:49,280
What?

264
00:22:00,480 --> 00:22:01,840
Our mission today...

265
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:03,040
is to fold all of them.

266
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:05,480
Write...

267
00:22:06,640 --> 00:22:07,920
my grandparents' names on yours.

268
00:22:09,400 --> 00:22:11,840
So it's for your grandparents.

269
00:22:13,840 --> 00:22:14,880
Then what are you writing on yours?

270
00:22:18,720 --> 00:22:20,000
I'll see it anyway.

271
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:24,960
I'm writing my own name.

272
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:30,000
Don't ask why.

273
00:25:00,600 --> 00:25:02,319
(October 7, 2010. She actually cooked for me today! I was happy.)

274
00:25:02,320 --> 00:25:03,599
(October 19, 2010. She made a new friend. This guy stinks.)

275
00:25:03,600 --> 00:25:05,719
(October 22, 2010. She swore at me for no reason.)

276
00:25:05,720 --> 00:25:07,240
(October 25, 2010. She wasn't home and didn't leave me money for food.)

277
00:25:09,120 --> 00:25:13,279
(November 12, 2010. She went out with a guy again and left me money.)

278
00:25:13,280 --> 00:25:14,999
(November 9, 2010. Ordered takeout. No fighting. A rare peaceful day.)

279
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:16,520
(October 30, 2010. She finally came home and was drunk.)

280
00:25:17,360 --> 00:25:18,879
(December 27, 2010. The jerk told me to buy beer and cigarettes.)

281
00:25:18,880 --> 00:25:20,240
(December 30, 2010. Aunt and that jerk ate like kings again.)

282
00:25:42,600 --> 00:25:46,159
(To-do list: See Master. Make up with Aunt.)

283
00:25:46,160 --> 00:25:47,280
(Write a will.)

284
00:26:21,680 --> 00:26:22,759
(To-do list: See Master. Make up with Aunt.)

285
00:26:22,760 --> 00:26:23,919
(Write a will.)

286
00:26:23,920 --> 00:26:25,119
(Rehome plushies.)

287
00:26:25,120 --> 00:26:26,480
(Find a new mentor for Celine.)

288
00:26:49,560 --> 00:26:50,560
You're awake?

289
00:27:00,080 --> 00:27:01,240
The food is ready.

290
00:27:04,440 --> 00:27:05,560
Did you cook this?

291
00:27:05,640 --> 00:27:06,640
Yes. Try it.

292
00:27:20,320 --> 00:27:21,960
I didn't expect you to be such a good cook.

293
00:27:23,040 --> 00:27:24,760
My mom never entered the kitchen when I was little.

294
00:27:25,440 --> 00:27:27,280
If I wanted to eat, I had to cook for myself.

295
00:27:28,120 --> 00:27:30,000
I could make scrambled eggs when I was five.

296
00:27:30,760 --> 00:27:32,480
The kitchen is like my bedroom.

297
00:27:37,600 --> 00:27:39,560
You don't want to be a part-time boyfriend...

298
00:27:39,640 --> 00:27:40,960
or a mechanic forever, right?

299
00:27:41,960 --> 00:27:45,480
How about I pay for you to open a cafe?

300
00:27:45,960 --> 00:27:48,840
You do something for me in return. It's a fair trade.

301
00:27:50,200 --> 00:27:53,360
No need for a trade. I enjoy talking to you.

302
00:27:54,320 --> 00:27:56,520
Besides, I quite like this job.

303
00:27:57,400 --> 00:27:59,000
Running a cafe is profitable now.

304
00:28:00,160 --> 00:28:02,160
It might pay better than being a part-time boyfriend.

305
00:28:04,040 --> 00:28:05,200
I'm not doing this for the money.

306
00:28:07,360 --> 00:28:09,240
You're a part-time boyfriend, but not for the money?

307
00:28:10,680 --> 00:28:11,920
I just want to make people happy.

308
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:14,760
I don't have many skills,

309
00:28:15,920 --> 00:28:17,080
but I'm a very good listener.

310
00:28:18,960 --> 00:28:20,800
So if you're ever unhappy,

311
00:28:22,560 --> 00:28:24,480
remember to tell me and don't keep it all inside.

312
00:28:25,240 --> 00:28:26,760
I'm on standby 24 hours a day.

313
00:28:38,680 --> 00:28:39,680
Hello.

314
00:28:43,080 --> 00:28:44,200
I'll think about it.

315
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:47,720
What is it?

316
00:28:49,200 --> 00:28:50,720
I looked into that village.

317
00:28:50,800 --> 00:28:53,160
There's a villager there whose background offers some clues.

318
00:28:54,800 --> 00:28:56,640
They might know the truth behind the attack on me.

319
00:28:58,760 --> 00:28:59,800
Then why aren't we going?

320
00:29:01,800 --> 00:29:03,720
I don't want to waste any more time on this.

321
00:29:05,280 --> 00:29:06,600
It doesn't seem that important anymore.

322
00:29:07,480 --> 00:29:08,840
What do you mean, not important?

323
00:29:08,920 --> 00:29:10,440
That person tried to kill you.

324
00:29:10,520 --> 00:29:11,880
We have to find them no matter what.

325
00:29:13,360 --> 00:29:15,480
I'll drive. It won't take long.

326
00:29:39,240 --> 00:29:41,280
I looked into Chiu Wing Tai again.

327
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:43,640
I found an employee at his company with the same name...

328
00:29:43,720 --> 00:29:45,840
as a registered villager in Chun Yat Village.

329
00:29:45,920 --> 00:29:48,000
Lee Chun Fun, 53 years old.

330
00:29:48,080 --> 00:29:50,200
She's the pantry lady at Chiu Wing Tai's company.

331
00:29:50,280 --> 00:29:51,680
She's in charge of cleaning and cooking.

332
00:29:52,920 --> 00:29:55,080
Isn't she the woman we met the other day?

333
00:29:55,880 --> 00:29:56,880
Could it be her?

334
00:29:58,040 --> 00:30:00,080
The person who attacked me was very skilled...

335
00:30:00,400 --> 00:30:02,640
and didn't look like a woman in her fifties at all.

336
00:30:05,240 --> 00:30:06,520
This happened just this morning.

337
00:30:06,840 --> 00:30:12,040
(Chiu Wing Tai's Male Partner Dies in Car Crash)

338
00:30:16,720 --> 00:30:18,280
Why do you think she's suspicious?

339
00:30:19,480 --> 00:30:21,360
I asked the employees at Nuen Lap.

340
00:30:21,440 --> 00:30:24,000
This Lee Chun Fun was very close to Chiu Wing Tai.

341
00:30:24,520 --> 00:30:26,080
She has a nephew who is a thug.

342
00:30:26,480 --> 00:30:27,480
Plus, the man in black...

343
00:30:27,560 --> 00:30:29,280
was last seen around here.

344
00:30:29,720 --> 00:30:31,120
So I think she knows something.

345
00:30:43,880 --> 00:30:47,080
You guys again? Haven't you found that person yet?

346
00:30:48,880 --> 00:30:49,960
We did, thanks.

347
00:30:52,680 --> 00:30:53,880
I recognize you.

348
00:30:54,320 --> 00:30:56,960
You're the lawyer who went against Mrs. Chiu.

349
00:30:57,840 --> 00:30:59,879
You looked familiar last time.

350
00:30:59,880 --> 00:31:00,960
I racked my brain for a long time.

351
00:31:02,240 --> 00:31:03,560
I finally remembered.

352
00:31:06,520 --> 00:31:07,520
Actually,

353
00:31:08,640 --> 00:31:10,400
I have something to tell you.

354
00:31:11,760 --> 00:31:12,760
What do you know?

355
00:31:19,600 --> 00:31:21,400
Were you attacked before?

356
00:31:22,960 --> 00:31:24,760
Why don't we talk inside my house?

357
00:31:29,080 --> 00:31:31,080
Come in, have a seat.

358
00:31:51,280 --> 00:31:52,480
Sorry, it's a bit messy.

359
00:32:00,520 --> 00:32:02,680
- Do you sleep upstairs? - Yes.

360
00:32:03,400 --> 00:32:04,880
Come in and sit down.

361
00:32:07,840 --> 00:32:09,800
I'll go make some tea for everyone.

362
00:32:19,120 --> 00:32:20,120
Here.

363
00:32:20,440 --> 00:32:22,880
Don't be shy. Have some tea.

364
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:25,000
Thank you.

365
00:32:38,440 --> 00:32:39,440
It's good.

366
00:32:40,720 --> 00:32:42,400
- What tea is this? - Chrysanthemum Pu-erh.

367
00:32:42,520 --> 00:32:44,920
It was Tai's favorite tea.

368
00:32:46,800 --> 00:32:49,080
I've worked for Tai since I was 18.

369
00:32:49,440 --> 00:32:51,360
Two years ago, I got lung cancer.

370
00:32:51,440 --> 00:32:53,800
I often missed work for chemotherapy.

371
00:32:53,880 --> 00:32:56,200
But Tai still paid me as usual.

372
00:32:56,280 --> 00:32:58,240
He told me not to worry about money.

373
00:32:58,760 --> 00:33:00,320
Where else can you find a boss like him?

374
00:33:00,400 --> 00:33:02,000
I decided to stay with him for life.

375
00:33:02,520 --> 00:33:05,640
So I would do anything he asked.

376
00:33:13,600 --> 00:33:15,240
How did you know I was attacked?

377
00:33:15,640 --> 00:33:18,280
I noticed an employee acting strange.

378
00:33:18,960 --> 00:33:20,120
I have his photo.

379
00:33:20,200 --> 00:33:21,560
I'll go upstairs and get it for you.

380
00:33:23,240 --> 00:33:24,280
Why are you helping me?

381
00:33:25,360 --> 00:33:27,480
You fulfilled Tai's final wish.

382
00:33:27,560 --> 00:33:28,960
Of course I'll help you.

383
00:33:40,480 --> 00:33:41,600
What's the plan?

384
00:33:43,720 --> 00:33:45,280
Let's see what she brings down first.

385
00:33:55,920 --> 00:33:57,200
They're downstairs.

386
00:33:57,760 --> 00:34:00,240
Sorry for troubling you to do it again.

387
00:34:00,840 --> 00:34:03,320
It's no trouble. It's only right.

388
00:34:35,800 --> 00:34:38,360
You can't leave.

389
00:34:55,440 --> 00:34:56,440
Go!

390
00:34:56,640 --> 00:34:57,880
Run!

391
00:35:45,320 --> 00:35:48,240
You wench, die!

392
00:36:02,840 --> 00:36:03,840
Hey!

393
00:36:04,760 --> 00:36:05,760
Hey!

394
00:36:06,320 --> 00:36:08,760
Where's Yam Yam?

395
00:36:10,760 --> 00:36:11,880
Where's Yam Yam?

396
00:36:18,960 --> 00:36:19,960
Amber.

397
00:36:20,240 --> 00:36:22,240
Amber!

398
00:36:22,800 --> 00:36:24,680
Amber, wake up.

399
00:36:24,800 --> 00:36:26,200
Amber, wake up!

400
00:36:44,680 --> 00:36:45,719
I clearly still have two days left.

401
00:36:45,720 --> 00:36:47,040
How could you bring me back down here?

402
00:36:47,120 --> 00:36:49,640
Please think about what happened before you speak.

403
00:36:49,720 --> 00:36:51,240
I didn't bring you down here.

404
00:36:51,320 --> 00:36:53,520
It's your karma that won't let you go.

405
00:36:53,680 --> 00:36:56,160
You're the King of Hell. You control life and death.

406
00:36:56,240 --> 00:36:58,720
My time isn't up yet. How could you let them mess around?

407
00:36:59,360 --> 00:37:00,960
I did let you return to the mortal world for a while.

408
00:37:01,040 --> 00:37:03,520
It's not my fault you insisted on coming back down.

409
00:37:04,560 --> 00:37:07,440
Anyway, I have two days left. Let me go back up now.

410
00:37:11,160 --> 00:37:12,520
According to the Book of Life and Death,

411
00:37:12,600 --> 00:37:14,400
you shouldn't be in the mortal world.

412
00:37:14,520 --> 00:37:16,000
I don't know what you're talking about.

413
00:37:17,760 --> 00:37:19,840
I have so much to do and so many people to see.

414
00:37:19,920 --> 00:37:21,160
I want to go back up.

415
00:37:21,840 --> 00:37:24,080
If you don't deal with the karma you've brought upon yourself,

416
00:37:24,160 --> 00:37:25,600
even if I let you go back,

417
00:37:25,680 --> 00:37:27,280
he'll still come for your life.

418
00:37:27,720 --> 00:37:29,960
You'll just keep going back and forth between life and death,

419
00:37:30,040 --> 00:37:31,440
until those two days are used up.

420
00:37:33,920 --> 00:37:35,320
Is Chiu Wing Tai my karma?

421
00:37:40,520 --> 00:37:42,080
If I resolve my karma,

422
00:37:42,160 --> 00:37:43,560
can I go back then?

423
00:37:43,640 --> 00:37:45,600
You can try if you want.

424
00:37:45,680 --> 00:37:48,600
But by the time you're done, those two days might be gone.

425
00:37:51,680 --> 00:37:52,680
Where is Chiu Wing Tai?

426
00:38:00,040 --> 00:38:01,880
Fine, I'll find him myself.

427
00:38:31,440 --> 00:38:32,640
Yau Yam Yam.

428
00:38:39,560 --> 00:38:40,560
Sign for this.

429
00:38:48,520 --> 00:38:50,920
I've opened a bank account for you down there.

430
00:38:51,760 --> 00:38:53,880
Everything in the netherworld costs money.

431
00:38:56,280 --> 00:38:57,320
This trunk is yours too.

432
00:39:02,080 --> 00:39:04,080
- So much money. - I'm so envious.

433
00:39:06,960 --> 00:39:08,639
- I'm so envious. - I've never seen so much money.

434
00:39:08,640 --> 00:39:10,960
I'm not dead yet. I'll be going back up soon.

435
00:39:11,040 --> 00:39:12,040
Take it back.

436
00:39:12,640 --> 00:39:14,440
If you're not dead, how could you be here?

437
00:39:14,520 --> 00:39:16,920
I'm just temporarily dead. Take it back.

438
00:39:19,960 --> 00:39:21,040
I'll keep this.

439
00:39:21,680 --> 00:39:23,480
You said you weren't dead.

440
00:39:31,200 --> 00:39:32,600
(On your first use, a photo will be automatically taken.)

441
00:39:38,160 --> 00:39:39,760
(Please write your living name in the blank space.)

442
00:39:46,280 --> 00:39:47,680
Listen up, ghosts!

443
00:39:48,800 --> 00:39:50,240
Who wants money?

444
00:39:50,800 --> 00:39:52,360
Who wants to get rich?

445
00:39:52,480 --> 00:39:55,320
- Of course I want money. - Who doesn't want money?

446
00:39:55,440 --> 00:39:58,560
I'm looking for a ghost named Chiu Wing Tai.

447
00:39:59,560 --> 00:40:03,600
Whoever finds him for me gets this stack of money.

448
00:40:04,360 --> 00:40:06,720
- Who's that? - How long has he been dead?
